Hello, \par
\par
In order to allow [serializejson] ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/SmartAudioTools/serializejson"}}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf3 https://github.com/SmartAudioTools/serializejson}}}\f0\fs22 ) to serialize dictionaries with no string keys,  and enable serializejson to be a drop-in replacement for the Python pickle package,  I wonder if it would be possible to add an option for automatically check if dictionaries contains only string keys, and call the "default" method if not instead of raising a "TypeError: keys must be strings" .\par
 \par
In the following code, I'm able to serialize a dictionary containing non string keys, by simulating call to default method for this dictionary. \par
\fs16\par
    from serializejson import dumps,loads\par
    \par
    def default(inst): \par
        if isinstance(inst,dict):\par
            return \{\par
                  "__class__":"__main__.dict_json_keys",\par
                  "__init__": \{dumps(key,indent=None):value for key, value in inst.items()\}\par
                 \} \par
        return inst\par
            \par
    def dict_json_keys(**args):\par
        return \{loads(key):value for key,value in args.items()\}\par
            \par
    obj = \{\par
            "string" : "str",\par
            b"bytes" : "bytes",\par
            True: "bool" , \par
            2 : "int",\par
            3.4 : "float",\par
            (5,6) : "tuple",\par
            frozenset([7,8]) : "frozenset"\par
        \}\par
    print(obj)\par
    """\{'string': 'str', b'bytes': 'bytes', True: 'bool', 2: 'int', 3.4: 'float', (5, 6): 'tuple', frozenset(\{8, 7\}): 'frozenset'\}"""\par
    \par
    dumped = dumps(default(obj))\par
    \par
    """\par
    \{\par
        "__class__": "__main__.dict_json_keys",\par
        "__init__": \{\par
                "\\"string\\"": "str",\par
                "2": "int",\par
               "3.4": "float",\par
                "true": "bool",\par
                "\{\\"__class__\\":\\"bytes\\",\\"__init__\\":[\\"bytes\\",\\"ascii\\"]\}": "bytes",\par
                "\{\\"__class__\\":\\"frozenset\\",\\"__init__\\":[8,7]\}": "frozenset",\par
                "\{\\"__class__\\":\\"tuple\\",\\"__init__\\":[5,6]\}": "tuple"\par
        \}\par
    \}\par
    """\par
    \par
    print(dumped)    \par
    loaded = loads(dumped,authorized_classes = [dict_json_keys])\par
    assert obj == loaded\par
